### ============================================================================
### Devices — HRIS Client (mobile) API
### ============================================================================
# Requires the VS Code "REST Client" extension (or a compatible .http runner).
#
# POST /api/devices only requires the caller to be logged in (no specific
# permission) — every employee can register their own device, same as
# GET /users/_current. Served by cmd/client (internal/bootstrap/client.go).
#
# How to run:
#   1. `make run-client` (defaults to port 9000, same as config.yml's
#      app.port — override APP_PORT if you're also running `make run-admin`
#      on this machine, they can't share a port).
#   2. Fill in @email / @password below.
#   3. Click "Send Request" on "Login" first. REST Client automatically stores
#      the `token` session cookie and replays it on every request below.
### ============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:9000/api
@email = admin@company.com
@password =Password123!

### ── Auth ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Login
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/_login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Logout
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/_logout


### ============================================================================
### Devices
### ============================================================================

### Register this device (called right after login)
POST {{baseUrl}}/devices
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "push_token": "ExponentPushToken[8LtzZrL-4suvWdevvDxdj3]",
  "device_id": "device-123",
  "app_version": "1.0.0",
  "provider": "expo",
  "platform": "android",
  "device_name": "Samsung A55"
}

### Re-register the same device (same push_token) — reassigns instead of duplicating
POST {{baseUrl}}/devices
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "push_token": "ExponentPushToken[xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx]",
  "device_id": "device-123",
  "app_version": "1.0.1",
  "provider": "expo",
  "platform": "android",
  "device_name": "Samsung A55"
}
